# <Study> — <topic> (TVBO replication)

**Replication** of <Author> et al., *<title>*, <venue> (<Year>). One declarative recipe
(`<Study>.yaml`) + minimal plotting; a *replication*, not a bit-exact reproduction (see
the report's scorecard). Backend chosen by fit — see `original_study/analysis/backend-fit.md`.

## Layout (FAIR)
```
<Study>/
  <Study>.yaml              one declarative recipe (all/selected experiments)
  original_study/           paper (version of record) + analysis/ (targets, figures, backend-fit)
  input/                    open data + DATA.md (provenance); processed connectome
  code/                     prepare_<study>.py, <study>_analysis.py (callables),
                            <study>_reference.py (verify), figures/plot.py
  figures/                  generated PNGs (fig0*, tvbo_fig*, ab_fig* A/B composites)
  output/                   run outputs — gitignored, regenerated by `tvbo run`
  report/                   report.qmd + report.pdf (computed numbers + scorecard)
```
## Reproduce
```bash
python code/prepare_<study>.py            # open data -> tvbo-ready Network
tvbo run <Study>.yaml -o output/nc        # all experiments in dependency order (add --experiment for a subset)
python code/figures/plot.py               # all figures + A/B composites
quarto render report/report.qmd --to pdf  # every number computed, no hardcoding
```
